Relevant columns and their possible use  
• `gsod2023.stn`, `gsod2022.stn` : station id – use to join with `stations.usaf`  
• `gsod2023.wban`, `gsod2022.wban` : WBAN id – second join key to make the match unique  
• `gsod2023.date`, `gsod2022.date` : day of observation – helps group by year if we ever need it (already split into `year`, `mo`, `da`)  
• `gsod2023.prcp`, `gsod2022.prcp` : daily precipitation in inches ( 99.99  = missing).  A “rainy day” = `prcp > 0 AND prcp <> 99.99`  
• `stations.state` : select only Washington stations (`'WA'`)  
• `stations.name` : human‑readable station name for the final list  

Typical conditions we will need  
```sql
WHERE prcp > 0            -- any measurable precipitation  
  AND prcp <> 99.99       -- skip the “missing” code  
```  
```sql
WHERE state = 'WA'        -- Washington State only
```  

Below are 10 illustrative BigQuery SQL statements (each limited to 20 rows) that progress from simple inspection to the complete answer.  
